;; The garage door box, built on the Pi 3 image that is known to boot.
;;
;; raspberrypi3-64-tailscale composed feature:tailscale onto the bare board
;; and produced a firmware rainbow screen with no kernel. This one composes
;; it onto raspberrypi3-64-bringup instead - the image that has been running
;; on this bench all week - so the only difference from something proven is
;; the tailscale package and the rootfs size.
;;
;; That makes it a test as well as a box: if this boots, the problem in the
;; other image was the bare-board composition or the 512M override, and we
;; know which by having changed one thing.
;;
;; The appliance daemons come along for the ride. On a board whose job is to
;; route a /32 to a garage relay they do nothing, and they cost a few hundred
;; kilobytes, which is a better trade than another twenty-minute build to
;; find out.
;;
;;   TS_AUTHKEY, TS_HOSTNAME, TS_ROUTES in /etc/default/tailscale
;;   approve the route in the admin console, then turn off key expiry
;;   use the relay's address: mDNS does not cross the tunnel

(image raspberrypi3-64-garage
  (compose
    image:raspberrypi3-64-bringup
    feature:tailscale
    feature:garage-relay)

  ;; 256M rather than the 512M the other image asked for: tailscaled and
  ;; tailscale are about 40MB together, and the appliance fits in 120M, so
  ;; this is generous without being a change worth suspecting.
  (override
    (value buildroot:BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE "256M"))

  ;; CI builds this one: it runs on a board in the house, doing a job.
  (ci build)

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16"))

  ;; The other half of this appliance: the ESP32 on the garage door itself.
  ;; Its broker address, its topics and its pins come from the same
  ;; composition that builds this image, so the two configurations cannot
  ;; disagree about how to reach each other.
  ;;
  ;;   silt esphome images/raspberrypi3-64-garage.sx -o garage.yaml
  ;;   esphome run garage.yaml
  ;;
  ;; silt does not build the firmware; esphome does, the way Buildroot builds
  ;; this image.
)
